  "summary": "Amsterdam first appears, as Amstelledamme, in a toll privilege issued by Count Floris V on 27 October 1275. A settlement formed by the Amstel estuary after the All Saints' Flood of 1170, and waterways let trade flourish. A canal district built from the late 16th century as a new port city reflects wealth from maritime trade.",
